Article 10 (Persons Setting Examination Questions, etc.)
(1) At least two persons shall prepare the questions for each written examination subject, and at least two examiners shall conduct interviews.
(2) Examination question setters or examiners shall be selected or commissioned from among the following persons by resolution of the Committee:
1. Professors of colleges of law (meaning persons serving as assistant professors or in higher positions at schools referred to in the subparagraphs of Article 2 of the Higher Education Act);
2. Judges;
3. Public prosecutors;
4. Military legal officers;
5. Persons possessing specialized knowledge or abilities relating to the examinations under Article 3.
(3) Allowances shall be paid to question setters or examiners within budgetary limits.
